# ourBride — Project Rules for Cursor

## 1. Project Structure
- Follow exact project folder structure. Case-sensitive.
- Folders: lowercase (pages, utils, store, lib), PascalCase for Components, Assets, Context, Hooks.
- Component folders must have index.ts for barrel export.
- No new folders/files unless instructed.

## 2. Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase, match file name (Button.tsx → Button)
- Props interfaces: PascalCase + Props (ButtonProps)
- Functions & variables: camelCase
- Constants: camelCase or UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- VariantProps: Use CVA pattern

## 3. Imports
- Use absolute imports with @/ alias.
- Import order: 1) external libs, 2) internal absolute, 3) relative, 4) type-only imports
- Exports: named exports preferred, default for pages only

## 4. UI / Tailwind Rules
- Use Tailwind CSS + design tokens only.
- Use cn() for class merging.
- Follow existing spacing, typography, colors, radius, shadows, breakpoints.
- Use CVA for all variant-based components.
- Reuse UI components only. No new design patterns unless instructed.
- *Insert regular comments between HTML/JSX elements*, e.g., <div> {/* comment */} </div>
- *Do not use inline/side comments at the end of lines*.

## 5. API Handling
- Use apiClient Axios instance only.
- React Query for all queries/mutations.
- Request interceptor: inject token from localStorage.
- Response interceptor: 401 → remove token, redirect /login.
- Do not call APIs directly in components.
- Follow existing naming patterns (useGetItems, useCreateItem, etc.)

## 6. Component Architecture
- Functional React components only.
- TypeScript strict mode.
- Use forwardRef + displayName if component accepts ref.
- Props exported separately.
- Support asChild pattern (Radix Slot) and composition.
- Use existing layout, UI, feature components.
- *JSDoc comments only for functions, hooks, and components*.
- Regular comments can be used in JSX/HTML.

## 7. Routing
- Use React Router v6 path + element format.
- Routes only in src/routes/routes.tsx.
- Protected routes: Redirect unauthenticated users.
- Use Link, useNavigate, useLocation.

## 8. Code Quality & Documentation
- ESLint + Prettier mandatory.
- No console.log in production.
- No dead code or unused imports.
- All functions, hooks, and components must have *JSDoc blocks*.
- JSX/HTML can have regular comments between elements.
- *No side-line/inline comments on the same line as code*.

## 9. Stricter Rules
- Never change filename casing.
- Never create new folder structures without instruction.
- Cursor must not modify existing logic unless explicitly instructed.
- Follow all Tailwind classes, design tokens, spacing, typography exactly.
- Reuse all existing utility components (Button, Input, Modal, etc.).
- All API calls must follow Axios + React Query setup.
- Do not introduce new design patterns unless instructed.